## Browse by task or configuration type

<% register = JSON.parse(File.read(File.join(root, 'data', 'ha-terminology.json'))) %>
<% sources = register['sources'].to_h { |source| [source['id'], source] } %>
<% categories = [['automation-language','Automations and scripts'], ['dashboard-language','Dashboard interactions'], ['assist-language','Assist and voice'], ['security-language','Accounts and security'], ['energy-language','Energy and quantities'], ['installation-language','Installation and maintenance'], ['settings-labels','Exact Settings destination names'], ['view-types','View layouts'], ['card-types','Card names and dispatch identifiers'], ['card-features','Card feature names'], ['selector-types','Selector identifiers']] %>
<ul><% categories.each do |category,title| %><li><a href="#<%= escape(category) %>"><%= escape(title) %></a></li><% end %></ul>

<% categories.each do |category,title| %>
<h2 id="<%= escape(category) %>"><%= escape(title) %></h2>
<% if category == 'settings-labels' %><p>These are the named destination labels in the checked Settings dashboard translation subtree. Keep the actual native translation in a different locale. A destination may be hidden or unavailable because of permissions, installation type or integration configuration.</p><% end %>
<% if category == 'card-types' %><p>All 71 native card dispatch identifiers are mapped. This includes strategy, error, startup and historical entries as well as public cards. The presence of a key is not evidence that it is a supported standalone editor choice, public extension API or maintained civica adapter.</p><% end %>
<% if category == 'card-features' %><p>All 53 feature registry keys are mapped. The compatible card and entity determine availability. Retain native capability checks, units, ranges and current state; do not invent operations from a feature name.</p><% end %>
<% if category == 'selector-types' %><p>All 61 frontend selector-dispatch keys are mapped. The public blueprint-selector documentation is a smaller, separate catalogue. These keys identify schema input types, including internal and compatibility entries; they are not labels to show as unexplained household questions.</p><% end %>
<% register['terms'].select { |term| term['category'] == category }.sort_by { |term| term['native_name'].downcase }.each do |term| %>
<details class="civica-audit-detail" id="<%= escape(term['id'].downcase) %>">
<summary><strong><%= escape(term['native_name']) %></strong><% if term['code_identifiers'] %> — <code><%= escape(term['code_identifiers'].join(', ')) %></code><% end %></summary>
<% if term['native_name_kind'] %><p><strong>Name source:</strong> <%= escape(term['native_name_kind']) %>.</p><% end %>
<p><strong>Household wording:</strong> <%= escape(term['household_wording']) %><%= '.' unless term['household_wording'].end_with?('.') %></p>
<p><strong>First-use explanation:</strong> <%= escape(term['first_use_explanation']) %></p>
<p><strong>Keep distinct:</strong> <%= escape(term['avoid_confusion']) %></p>
<% if term['code_kind'] %><p><strong>Technical value scope:</strong> <%= escape(term['code_kind']) %>.</p><% end %>
<p>Reference: <code><%= escape(term['id']) %></code>. <% term['source_ids'].each_with_index do |source_id,index| %><%= ' · ' unless index.zero? %><a href="<%= escape(sources.fetch(source_id)['url']) %>"><%= escape(sources.fetch(source_id)['title']) %></a><% end %>.</p>
<% if term['native_label_pointer'] %><p><strong>Source label pointer:</strong> <code><%= escape(term['native_label_pointer']) %></code>.</p><% end %>
</details>
<% end %>
<% end %>

## Review instructions against the actual installation

For this checked frontend, **Tools** is the Settings destination for diagnostic tools and **Apps** is the current additional-software label. Older material may say Developer tools or Add-ons. Current action instructions may also differ from older Services wording. Update a navigation instruction only after verifying the actual destination and supported version; keep backend `service` fields, historical quotations and saved configuration literal.

An exact English source string may use a spelling such as “Color”. Preserve it when identifying that control, while using ordinary UK English “colour” in civica's explanation. Do not silently rewrite native labels to satisfy a prose preference or invent a translation for another language.

Read [the terminology scope and maintenance process](home-assistant-terminology.html) for the explicit denominators and source freshness record. Use [native compatibility guidance](../home-assistant/compatibility-register.html) before claiming a live adapter or installed capability. This reference is writing guidance, not a new execution or permission layer.
